language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_028_bibd: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Generate a balanced incomplete block design (BIBD) with parameters (v, b, r, k, lambda): arrange v distinct objects into b blocks so that each block contains exactly k distinct objects, each object occurs in exactly r different blocks, and every two distinct objects occur together in exactly lambda blocks. The design is given as its v by b incidence matrix, with exactly r ones per row, k ones per column, and a scalar product of lambda between any two distinct rows.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_028_bibd.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_028_bibd.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_028_bibd_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_028_bibd.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_028_bibd_1.param -run-solver

$ v: number of objects
given v : int
$ b: number of blocks
given b : int
$ r: number of blocks each object occurs in
given r : int
$ k: number of distinct objects in each block
given k : int
$ l: number of blocks in which every two distinct objects occur together (lambda)
given l : int

$ matrix[i,j]: object i is in block j (indices 1-based; the data's index 0 is 1). Named matrix_ because matrix is an Essence' word.
find matrix_ : matrix indexed by [int(1..v), int(1..b)] of bool

branching on [matrix_]
such that
$ each object occurs in exactly r blocks
forAll i : int(1..v) . ((sum j : int(1..b) . toInt(matrix_[i,j])) = r),
$ each block contains exactly k distinct objects
forAll j : int(1..b) . ((sum i : int(1..v) . toInt(matrix_[i,j])) = k),
$ every two distinct objects occur together in exactly lambda blocks
forAll i : int(1..v) . forAll i2 : int(i+1..v) . ((sum j : int(1..b) . toInt(matrix_[i,j] /\ matrix_[i2,j])) = l)
